  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the Urgent and Ongoing Humanitarian Needs of War-Affected Populations in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two years on from the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation on 24 February 2022, the war continues; ravaging frontline communities, causing forced displacement and family separation, resulting in ongoing humanitarian needs. The International Organization for Migration (IOM)&#x2019;s 2024 Humanitarian Support project will support minimum living standards and reduce barriers to access for war-affected populations in Ukraine by providing lifesaving assistance to vulnerable populations through a multi-sectoral response, including activities falling under the Inter-Agency Standing Committee (IASC) sectors of Shelter/Non-food Items, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene, Multipurpose Cash Assistance, Protection and Health/Mental Health and Psychosocial Support, and Humanitarian Coordination, Information Management and Assessments.</narrative>
  </description>
